# Finding E5 (lockstep lines, reanimator-02): Animate Dead leaves the battlefield before its enters ability resolved.
# Forge models "When Animate Dead leaves the battlefield, that creature's controller sacrifices it" as a delayed trigger created when the
# enters ability resolves (animate_dead.txt: DBDelay), so with the target gone it never exists and only the enters trigger is on the stack.
# The engine has it as a separate triggered ability (legacy.cards.ron), so Animate Dead going to the graveyard puts a second, empty trigger on the stack.
# Effect on play: one extra stack object and priority window, no change in the game result. The Oracle text keeps the sentence inside the one ability.
=== animate-dead-leaves-before-etb-resolves
title: Surgical Extraction exiles the target while Animate Dead's enters trigger is on the stack: one trigger left (the enters trigger)
ref: Animate Dead Oracle; CR 603.7, 608.2b, 704.5m
state:
  humanhand=Animate Dead
  humanbattlefield=Swamp;Swamp
  humangraveyard=Griselbrand
  aihand=Surgical Extraction
script:
  p1: cast Animate Dead -> Griselbrand
  p1: pass
  p2: pass
  p1: pass
  p2: cast Surgical Extraction -> Griselbrand
  p2: pass
  p1: pass
  p1: check stack size == 1
expect:
  zone p1 exile has "Griselbrand"
  zone p1 graveyard has "Animate Dead"
